              "title": "Initialize the Community Project",
              "prompt": "The terminal opens inside `community-project/`. The folder contains only `README.md` and `schedule.txt`, and it is not a Git repository yet. Initialize the current folder as a repository whose first branch is `main`. Do not edit or stage either file.",
              "hint": "Create repository metadata in the current folder and name the first branch `main`.",
              "help": {
                "concept": "`git init -b main` creates the hidden `.git` metadata directory in the current folder and chooses `main` as the first branch. It does not edit, stage, or commit the project files.",
                "hint_1": "The terminal is already at the project root, so no `cd` command is needed.",
                "hint_2": "The result should be a repository with zero commits and two untracked files."
              },
              "starterCode": "# Community Project\n\nShared community activities and updates.\n",
              "solutionCode": "git init -b main",
              "instructions": "The terminal opens inside `community-project/`. The folder contains only `README.md` and `schedule.txt`, and it is not a Git repository yet. Initialize the current folder as a repository whose first branch is `main`. Do not edit or stage either file.",
