              "title": "Remove the Obsolete Contact List",
              "prompt": "Remove the tracked file by running:\n\n```bash\ngit rm contacts.txt\n```\n\nThis command deletes `contacts.txt` from the working tree and stages its removal in one action.\n\nThen inspect all staged path changes by running:\n\n```bash\ngit diff --staged --name-status\n```\n\nThe summary should show the removal of `contacts.txt` together with the staged rename from `schedule.txt` to `events.txt`. Git uses status letters such as `D` for a deleted file and `R` when it recognizes a likely rename.\n\nLeave both staged changes uncommitted.\n",
              "hint": "Stage the tracked removal and review both structural changes.",
              "help": {
                "concept": "`git rm contacts.txt` deletes the working file and stages its removal. `git diff --staged --name-status` summarizes staged path changes with status letters such as `D` for deletion and `R` for a likely rename.",
                "hint_1": "Do not remove `README.md` or `events.txt`.",
                "hint_2": "The summary should contain the rename and the contact removal."
              },
