            "title": "Input, Processing, Output (Using Your Workspace)",
            "bodyMarkdown": "Before we go further, I want to take a moment to familiarize you with your workspace.\n\n> **Note:** These instructions are written for **desktop** users. If you’re on a **phone or tablet**, or depending on how **wide your screen** is, the layout may look a little different.\n\nLet’s start on the **left side**: this is your **module sidebar**. You can navigate between sections by selecting one of the tiles.\n\nOn the **right**, you have your **code editor**.\n\nNow take a look at the layout: you have the editor, where you will type your code, and the terminal right below it, where the output from `print()` and any errors will usually appear.\n\nClick the **Run** button (the triangle icon) in the **top-right corner** of your code editor and confirm that the text inside the quotes is printed in the terminal.\n\nCongratulations — you just learned how to run your code and display output in the terminal.\n\nNow copy this code, erase the current one, and run it again:\n\n~~~python\nprint(\"I am learning Python\")\n~~~\n\nVerify that it also appears in the terminal.\n\nWhen you finish, move on to the next topic and make sure you mark everything as read."
