    "m0_s04_students_explorer_project": {
      "title": "Explore the students table",
      "prompt": "Use the SQL workspace on the right to explore the `students` table.\n\nFor each task:\n\n1. type the query in the editor\n2. click **Run**\n3. read the **Results** tab\n4. optionally click **Tables** to remind yourself what table exists\n\nTasks:\n\n1. Return a message using:\n   `SELECT 'Ready to query' AS message;`\n2. Show all columns and rows from `students`\n3. Show only the `name` and `grade` columns\n4. Show only students with grade `A`\n5. Sort the full table by `name`\n\nRun one query at a time.\nDo not paste them all together.\nThis project is about using the workspace confidently.",
      "help": {
        "concept": "This project trains the full workflow: write a query, run it, inspect the result, then try the next query.",
        "hint_1": "You will likely use `SELECT 'Ready to query' AS message;`, `SELECT *`, `SELECT name, grade`, `WHERE grade = 'A'`, and `ORDER BY name`.",
        "hint_2": "A good sequence is:\n```sql\nSELECT 'Ready to query' AS message;\nSELECT * FROM students;\nSELECT name, grade FROM students;\nSELECT * FROM students WHERE grade = 'A';\nSELECT * FROM students ORDER BY name;\n```\nRun them one at a time."
      },
      "hint": "Use one small query at a time.",
      "starterCode": "-- Task 1\n-- Return a message in the Results tab\n\n",
      "fixedLanguage": "sql",
      "fixedSqlDialect": "sqlite",
      "runtime": {
        "kind": "sql",
        "datasetId": "students_intro",
        "resultShape": "table"
      }
    },
